class=\"minimap_wp minimap_w\"></div></div></div></div>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"minimap mobile-hidden minimap-zoom-2\" style=\"overflow:hidden;display: inline-block;\"><div style=\"overflow:hidden; border: #3366CC 1px solid; position:relative; display: block;image-rendering: crisp-edges;image-rendering: optimizeSpeed;image-rendering: -moz-crisp-edges;image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;image-rendering: pixelated;-ms-interpolation-mode: nearest-neighbor;width: 153px; height: 153px;\">\n<div class=\"map_image_crop mobile-hidden\" style=\"overflow:hidden; position:absolute; top: -823px;left:-2239px;clip:rect(823px 2392px 976px 2239px);\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Minimap Floor 11\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"4096\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Minimap_Floor_11_72a054.png\" width=\"5120\"/></span></span>\n<div style=\"overflow:hidden;position:absolute; width:11px; height: 11px; left:2328px; top:922px; z-index:10;\"><div style=\"position:absolute; left:-22px; top:-11px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Minimap Symbols\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"22\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Minimap_Symbols_48c2de.gif\" width=\"121\"/></span></span></div></div>\n<div style=\"overflow:hidden;position:absolute; width:11px; height: 11px; left:2292px; top:876px; z-index:10;\"><div style=\"position:absolute; left:-33px; top:0px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Minimap Symbols\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"22\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Minimap_Symbols_48c2de.gif\" width=\"121\"/></span></span></div></div>\n<p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p><p><br/>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n</div><div style=\"text-align:right;background-color:#DDDDDD;padding:0px 3px;\"><div class=\"minimap_clic\"><a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"32902,31426,11\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">Browse Map (32902, 31426, 11)</a><div class=\"minimap_wp minimap_w\"></div></div></div></div>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</center>\n<p>Talk to her about a <span class=\"keyword-highlight\">shaman</span> you need to kill, and she'll tell you need to kill it from the inside, getting swallowed him, and then destroying his vile heart.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-The_Belly_of_the_Beast\">The Belly of the Beast</span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i><b>Note:</b> This mission can be risky due to damage reflection and agony damage. Be cautious if you are unsure whether you can survive the damage or not, and avoid attacking in area. It has a time limit of 10 minutes, players will get kicked after the time has passed.</i></dd></dl>\n<p>Enter the room to the east and step on the blood pool; you'll got to a lever room for the last mission to destroy the shaman's heart.\n</p><p>Here your goal is to go through the room while surviving the creatures there, then destroying the <a href=\"#/wiki/Vampiric%20Heart\">Vampiric Heart</a> located at the very end of the room.\n</p><p>There are your enemies in this mission:\n</p>\n<center>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\">Creature</th>\n<th>Notes\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"#/wiki/Digestive%20Fluid\">Digestive Fluid</a></td>\n<td><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Digestive%20Fluid\"><img alt=\"Digestive Fluid\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Digestive_Fluid_f135f0.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\"><ul><li>Deals damage to a player who steps on it</li><li>Temporarily disappears, so can be avoided</li></ul>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"#/wiki/Vampiric%20Flesh\">Vampiric Flesh</a></td>\n<td><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Vampiric%20Flesh\"><img alt=\"Vampiric Flesh\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Vampiric_Flesh_c997f7.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\"><ul><li>Reflects damage inflicted to it (avoid attacking many at the same time)</li></ul>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"#/wiki/Digestive%20Ooze\">Digestive Ooze</a></td>\n<td><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Digestive%20Ooze\"><img alt=\"Digestive Ooze\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Digestive_Ooze_448d57.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\"><ul><li>Regular creatures attacking in melee range</li><li>Respawn quickly after getting killed</li></ul>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"#/wiki/Vampiric%20Heart\">Vampiric Heart</a></td>\n<td><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Vampiric%20Heart\"><img alt=\"Vampiric Heart\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Vampiric_Heart_49c211.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\"><ul><li>Immobile creature with all effects from the other creatures</li><li>Its constant earth AoE attack has maximum range of 4 tiles, so shooters can stand at range 5 to attack it; this will also help to avoid digestive fluid in the room</li><li>If you and your team are struggling to attack the heart while tanking oozees, it could be a good idea to lure them away first</li></ul>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</center>\n<p>Once the heart is destroyed you receive a questlog update message. Leave through the teleport located south from where the heart was, and report to Anaztassja.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-The_Father_of_Vampires\">The Father of Vampires</span></h2>\n<p>Anaztassja tells you it's time to face the usurper vampire to finally destroy him once and for all. Enter the room to the west, and be ready!\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Vladrukh\">Vladrukh</span></h3>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Vladrukh\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Vladrukh_c66aec.gif\" width=\"64\"/><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"fight-tips\" style=\"color:black;border: 1px solid #cccccc;border-radius: 4px;width:auto;background-color:#ecf0f4;margin: 5px 5px 0 0;padding-left:2px;display:table;\"><small><b>Battle recommendations:</b></small><br/>\n<div class=\"tooltip\">\n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Life%20Drain\"><img alt=\"Life Drain Protection Icon\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"38\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Life_Drain_Protection_Icon_69a02f.gif\" width=\"38\"/></a></span><div class=\"tooltiptext\"><span>Equip Life Drain Damage<b> Protection</b> during this fight. </span></div></div><div class=\"tooltip\">\n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Earth Protection Icon\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"38\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Earth_Protection_Icon_733cb1.gif\" width=\"38\"/></span><div class=\"tooltiptext\"><span>Equip Earth Damage<b> Protection</b> during this fight. </span></div></div>\n</div>\n<p>The fight is essentially split into two different phases: one where Vladrukh is actually present in the room and you attack him, and a second one where you need to kill essences to bring the boss back to the fight. These phases repeat themselves alternately until the end of the fight.\n</p><p>In the first phase (also the starting phase as you enter the room), Vladrukh will be in the room and shortly after three <a href=\"#/wiki/Blood%20Pool\">Blood Pools</a> will spawn. Different teams handle this phase differently, depending what is more feasible for their level, or preference but in general the <a href=\"#/wiki/Knight\">Knight</a> will want to lure the boss to a corner, facing a direction where the boss doesn't hit shooters with his frequent waves. In this phase you and your team have about 2 minutes and 20 seconds to attack the boss.\n</p><p>As for the pools, shooters can choose to tank them, but a safer approach is luring them away from the boss and having a mage summon <a href=\"#/wiki/Demon%20Skeleton\">Demon Skeletons</a> to block them. Pools attack exclusively with <a href=\"#/wiki/Life%20Drain\">Life Drain</a> damage, and since demon skeletons are immune to it, it makes them perfect summons for the task.\n</p><p>After the 2 minutes and 20 seconds mark, Vladrukh will disappear and new creatures will appears in the room: four <a href=\"#/wiki/Vampire%20Bat\">Vampire Bats</a> and four <a href=\"#/wiki/Vampiric%20Essence\">Vampiric Essences</a> (the <a href=\"#/wiki/Blood%20Pool\">Blood Pools</a> don't disappear!). Your goal now is to kill the four Vampiric Essences as fast as you can so you can go back to the first phase where you can attack Vladrukh. It's also important to deal with this second phase fast because Vladrukh heals himself while you're busy dealing with the essences.\n</p><p>Be aware that <a href=\"#/wiki/Vampire%20Bat\">Vampire Bats</a> can be quite dangerous. They are immortal, make you <a href=\"#/wiki/Drunk\">drunk</a>, cause <a href=\"#/wiki/Feared\">fear</a>, reflect all damages inflicted to them, and also don't respect <a href=\"#/wiki/Knight\">Knight</a>'s <a href=\"#/wiki/Challenge\">Challenge</a>. Their weakness is that they don't sense invisibility, so prepare to put <a href=\"#/wiki/Stealth%20Ring\">Stealth Rings</a> or cast <a href=\"#/wiki/Invisible\">Invisible</a>]] as soon as they appear.\n</p><p>Repeat these phases until the boss reaches red HP. Now Vladrukh gets an additional temporary form that turns him into a poison field for few seconds. In that form it becomes immortal and deals considerably more damage than normal. <a href=\"#/wiki/Knight\">Knights</a> can use these few seconds to run the boss around (as long as it's safe for him and shooters; don't forget the boss waves very frequently!) then trap him again. This is essentially an additional mechanic to delay your progress when the boss is low in health.\n</p><p>Keep on dealing damage until the boss is dead.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Reward_2\">Reward</span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Gloom Maw (Mount)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Gloom_Maw_Mount_1ce01a.gif\" width=\"64\"/><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>After defeating <a href=\"#/wiki/Vladrukh\">Vladrukh</a>, report a last time to <a href=\"#/wiki/Anaztassja%20Moroia\">Anaztassja Moroia</a> and you will receive the <a href=\"#/wiki/Gloom%20Maw%20%28Mount%29\">Gloom Maw (Mount)</a> and <span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Achievement Grade Symbol\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"18\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Achievement_Grade_Symbol_75a6f6.gif\" width=\"18\"/></span> <a href=\"#/wiki/Bat%20Person\">Bat Person</a> achievement. Also, you're now allowed to use the Mysterious Machine on the highest floor, which teleports you to the entrance of the fortress.\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>","quests":[]}